{"path":"s48","heading":"Conditions for enforcement of foreign awards.","in_1996":true,"nodes_1996":[{"path":"s48","node_type":"section","number":"48","heading":"Conditions for enforcement of foreign awards.","text":""},{"path":"s48.ss1","node_type":"subsection","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"Enforcement of a foreign award may be refused, at the request of the party against whom it is invoked, only if that party furnishes to the court proof that—"},{"path":"s48.ss1.cl(a)","node_type":"clause","number":"a","heading":null,"text":"the parties to the agreement referred to in section 44 were, under the law applicable to them, under some incapacity, or the said agreement is not valid under the law to which the parties have subjected it or, failing any indication thereon, under the law of the country where the award was made; or"},{"path":"s48.ss1.cl(b)","node_type":"clause","number":"b","heading":null,"text":"the party against whom the award is invoked was not given proper notice of the appointment of the arbitrator or of the arbitral proceedings or was otherwise unable to present his case; or"},{"path":"s48.ss1.cl(c)","node_type":"clause","number":"c","heading":null,"text":"the award deals with a difference not contemplated by or not falling within the terms of the submission to arbitration, or it contains decisions on matters beyond the scope of the submission to arbitration:"},{"path":"s48.ss1.cl(c).p1","node_type":"proviso","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"Provided that, if the decisions on matters submitted to arbitration can be separated from those not so submitted, that part of the award which contains decisions on matters submitted to arbitration may be enforced; or"},{"path":"s48.ss1.cl(d)","node_type":"clause","number":"d","heading":null,"text":"the composition of the arbitral authority or the arbitral procedure was not in accordance with the agreement of the parties, or, failing such agreement, was not in accordance with the law of the country where the arbitration took place; or"},{"path":"s48.ss1.cl(e)","node_type":"clause","number":"e","heading":null,"text":"the award has not yet become binding on the parties, or has been set aside or suspended by a competent authority of the country in which, or under the law of which, that award was made."},{"path":"s48.ss2","node_type":"subsection","number":"2","heading":null,"text":"Enforcement of an arbitral award may also be refused if the Court finds that—"},{"path":"s48.ss2.cl(a)","node_type":"clause","number":"a","heading":null,"text":"the subject-matter of the difference is not capable of settlement by arbitration under the law of India; or"},{"path":"s48.ss2.cl(b)","node_type":"clause","number":"b","heading":null,"text":"the enforcement of the award would be contrary to the public policy of India."},{"path":"s48.ss2.expl1","node_type":"explanation","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"Without prejudice to the generality of clause (b), it is hereby declared, for the avoidance of any doubt, that an award is in conflict with the public policy of India if the making of the award was induced or affected by fraud or corruption."},{"path":"s48.ss3","node_type":"subsection","number":"3","heading":null,"text":"If an application for the setting aside or suspension of the award has been made to a competent authority referred to in clause (e) of sub-section (1) the Court may, if it considers it proper, adjourn the decision on the enforcement of the award and may also, on the application of the party claiming enforcement of the award, order the other party to give suitable security."}],"events":[{"instrument":"3/2016","title":"Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2015 (No. 3 of 2016)","effective":"from 23 Oct 2015 (Ordinance 9 of 2015)","edges":[{"instrument":"3/2016","old":"s48.ss2.expl1","new":"s48.ss2.expl1","op_type":"substitute","source":"agent","group":"3/2016|s22","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"New explanation retains core substance of old explanation, thus descends from it."},{"instrument":"3/2016","old":null,"new":"s48.ss2.expl2","op_type":"insert","source":"agent","group":"3/2016|s22","confidence":0.9,"rationale":"No counterpart in old units; new explanation added."}],"instructions":{"3/2016|s22":"In section 48 of the principal Act, for the Explanation to sub-section (2), the following Explanations shall be substituted, namely:— “Explanation 1.—For the avoidance of any doubt, it is clarified that an award is in conflict with the public policy of India, only if,— (i) the making of the award was induced or affected by fraud or corruption or was in violation of section 75 or section 81; or (ii) it is in contravention with the fundamental policy of Indian law; or (iii) it is in conflict with the most basic notions of morality or justice. Explanation 2.—For the avoidance of doubt, the test as to whether there is a contravention with the fundamental policy of Indian law shall not entail a review on the merits of the dispute.”."},"intent":[{"unit":"3/2016|s22","status":"not_determinable","claim":"intent not determinable from available record","tier":null,"quote":null,"document_id":null,"span":null,"attribution":null,"tiers_searched":["sor","sor","debate","debate","report"]}]}]}